+## Adaptive worker frontier and mutation ownership
+
+Use all available bounded-worker capacity for useful independent work; refill slots as workers finish. Frontier critics are read-only. Existing designated task implementers may edit only task-owned paths in isolated worktrees; one integration owner alone stages, commits, pushes, mutates issues/threads, merges, publishes evidence, and closes lifecycle state. Never dispatch competing writers or let worker count dilute that authority.
+
+While an implementer owns the task files, parallel critics may derive adversarial tests, inspect adapter/provider shapes, model security and TOCTOU failures, or review compatibility. Freeze the reviewed bytes first and return findings in this compact contract:
+
+```text
+packet_ref: COMMIT:<full 40-character SHA> | SNAPSHOT:<sha256 of retained patch/artifacts>
+authority: PROTECTED | ADVISORY
+role: <bounded role>
+verdict: PASS | REQUEST_CHANGES
+finding: <invariant> | <severity> | <evidence> | <minimal counterexample> | <suggested test> | <mutation scope> | <confidence>
+```
+
+Only `COMMIT` + `PROTECTED` may produce shipping approval. A `SNAPSHOT` packet is immutable pre-commit exploration, remains advisory, and must retain the hashed patch/artifacts; the mutable current checkout is never a review identity.
+
+Deduplicate by invariant plus counterexample. A supported blocker wins regardless of PASS count. Mandatory roles complete; exploratory waves stop after two successive waves add no evidence-supported blocker/high/medium invariant; unsupported or low-confidence suggestions do not extend the frontier. The integration owner accepts/rejects findings with reasons and applies one converged patch set.
+
+Maintain a **changed-surface validation manifest** in the work artifacts: exact focused tests, lint targets, type/security checks, and diff checks. Do not replace it with a wildcard suite that drags in known unrelated platform/daemon failures. Preserve any broad failure as evidence; never infer a pass from timeout or partial output.
+
+The existing spec-before-quality gate still applies per task. Parallel critics supply evidence to that sequence; they do not turn quality review into a race against unfinished spec review.
+
+---
