+# Release Critical-Path Swarm Decisions
+
+## D1 — Optimize discovery latency, not gate latency
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Protected CI, exact-SHA review, settle, ownership, serial merge, and exact-merge verification are mandatory. Efficiency work targets late discovery, repeated head invalidation, redundant broad validation, manual observation, and non-durable continuation.
+
+## D2 — Use all available bounded-worker capacity
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Low-cost workers are not conserved. Fill every available slot with a distinct bounded role and refill immediately while useful uncovered roles remain. Runtime concurrency limits are execution constraints, not target widths.
+
+## D3 — Adaptive waves replace fixed reviewer counts
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Mandatory roles always complete. Exploratory waves continue until two successive waves yield no new blocker/high/medium invariant. This prevents both arbitrary under-review and endless duplicate fan-out.
+
+## D4 — Role evidence beats majority voting
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+A single well-supported blocker is sufficient. Ten generic PASS votes do not override a concrete counterexample. Findings are keyed by invariant, evidence, and minimal counterexample.
+
+## D5 — One integration authority owns durable mutation
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Many workers inspect, model threats, derive tests, and review. Existing designated task implementers may edit only task-owned paths in isolated worktrees. One integration authority alone stages, commits, pushes, mutates issues/threads, merges, publishes evidence, and closes lifecycle state.
+
+## D6 — Harvest same-head feedback before amendment
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Do not amend for the first arriving review comment while required same-head reviewers are still active. Enumerate required and optional channels at packet creation. A required unavailable channel fails closed; an optional unavailable worker gets one bounded retry but cannot hold the barrier forever or count as approval. Batch valid findings where possible. Findings introduced by remediation still require a new exact-head cycle.
+
+## D7 — Gate contradictions are control-plane incidents
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+After one reconciliation pull, a persistent impossible verdict is not normal PR feedback. At 15 minutes it is explicitly recorded as a control-plane incident with retained operands and runtime versions.
+
+## D8 — Candidate gate code cannot self-authorize
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+A broken installed merge authority is repaired in an isolated stable-base control-plane lane. That lane is independently reviewed, merged, verified, and activated before the product lane resumes.
+
+## D9 — All evidence is retained and replayable
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Worker outputs, exact diffs, focused test output, provider payload shapes, and Shepherd operands are stored as artifacts. A command exit code without retained output is not sufficient evidence.
+
+## D10 — Forge skills are product authority
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+The efficiency contract must live in canonical `skills/*` and byte-identical `.agents/skills/*` mirrors. Updating only an assistant-local skill is insufficient for Forge users and teammates.
+
+## D11 — Review identity is immutable bytes, never a checkout label
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Protected approval binds only to `COMMIT:<full 40-character SHA>`. Pre-commit exploration may bind to `SNAPSHOT:<sha256>` when the exact patch/artifacts are retained, but it is advisory. A mutable `WORKTREE` label can never identify reviewed content or satisfy a shipping gate.
+
+## D12 — Current handoff remains explicit until the controller exists
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+Shepherd stops at `MERGE_READY`. Until a durable transition controller is installed, one named coordinator must re-prove Kernel ownership, re-read exact head and gates, execute the actor-scoped Forge merge command, verify the exact merge, publish evidence, and close the matching issue. No live coordinator means a safe stop, not implied continuation.
