+# Release Critical-Path Swarm Implementation Plan
+
+> **For Hermes:** Use subagent-driven-development to execute the tasks. Fill every available bounded-worker slot, but preserve one integration writer per overlapping surface.
+
+**Goal:** Collapse the elapsed time from implementation-ready to verified merge by moving discovery before the first protected head, batching same-head feedback, and making safe transitions durable and system-owned.
+
+**Architecture:** Forge compiles each candidate head into an immutable review packet, fans it through adaptive role-based worker waves, and converges structured findings by invariant. Shepherd remains the verdict source; a separate durable transition controller leases idempotent actions after rechecking head, ownership, reviews, CI, settle, and issue state. Candidate gate code never authorizes its own merge.
+
+**Tech stack:** Forge Kernel events/claims, Shepherd bundles and journal, JavaScript/Bun tests, Markdown skills, Git/GitHub protected checks.
+
+---
+
+## Evidence and diagnosis
+
+Measured GitHub data for the S0 train:
+
+- PR #469: 2 commits; opened `2026-07-31T11:46:05Z`; merged `13:52:20Z` — about 2h06m.
+- PR #470: 4 commits; opened `14:22:01Z`; merged `17:40:03Z` — about 3h18m, including ordered-queue wait behind #469.
+- PR #471: opened `14:22:42Z`; 7 pushed commits through `19:38:24Z`; 11 review objects; last protected check completed `19:56:09Z`.
+- The prolonged #471 work after protected CI was release-control-plane diagnosis and repair, not feature implementation.
+
+The dominant latency is therefore late discovery and exact-head invalidation, not code-writing speed. Every amendment invalidates prior review, triggers protected CI, and restarts settle. Opening non-next-at-bat PRs as ready also creates deliberately stale reviews and checks.
+
+## Critical-path compiler
+
+### 1. Immutable review packet
+
+For each candidate head, retain:
+
+- repository, PR, base SHA, exact 40-character head SHA;
+- exact diff and changed-file manifest;
+- acceptance criteria and explicit invariants;
+- focused validation commands and retained output artifacts;
+- runtime/tool/provider versions;
+- captured Shepherd operand bundle and verdict;
+- configured reviewer roles and completion state.
+
+Every worker receives the same packet. No reviewer reconstructs mutable state independently unless its assigned role is live-source verification.
+
+### 2. Adaptive role waves
+
+Fill all available bounded-worker slots with distinct roles. Initial roles:
+
+1. requirements/spec compliance;
+2. adversarial state-machine and false-clean analysis;
+3. change-class edge-case and mutation-test generation;
+4. adapter/API/provider-shape fidelity;
+5. security/identity/lease/TOCTOU review;
+6. compatibility/platform/line-ending review;
+7. test-quality and false-positive/false-negative review;
+8. operational/controller recovery review;
+9. documentation/runbook/drift review;
+10. latency-critical-path and redundant-work audit.
+
+As a slot completes, refill it with the highest-value uncovered role. A wave returns structured findings:
+
+```json
+{
+  "packet_sha": "<exact head>",
+  "role": "<bounded role>",
+  "verdict": "PASS|REQUEST_CHANGES",
+  "findings": [{
+    "invariant": "<stable key>",
+    "severity": "blocker|high|medium|low",
+    "evidence": "<file/line, fixture, or retained operand>",
+    "counterexample": "<minimal failing scenario>",
+    "suggested_test": "<test name and assertion>",
+    "mutation_scope": ["<files>"],
+    "confidence": "high|medium|low"
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+Convergence is role-based, not majority voting. A single supported blocker wins. Duplicate findings collapse by invariant plus counterexample. Stop only when all mandatory roles complete and two successive exploratory waves yield no new blocker/high/medium invariant. Low-confidence duplicates do not extend the frontier.
+
+### 3. Single-writer remediation
+
+Reviewers do not mutate shared files. The Sol integration owner:
+
+- validates/deduplicates findings;
+- records accepted/rejected reasoning;
+- assigns non-overlapping patches to isolated writers only when file ownership is disjoint;
+- applies or merges one converged remediation batch;
+- regenerates the exact packet for the amended head.
+
+### 4. Review-harvest barrier
+
+Do not amend for the first arriving bot comment while configured same-head reviewers are still active. Wait for all required same-head checks/reviewers to reach terminal state, then apply one batch where possible. A finding caused by that batch still requires a new round; an uncollected old-head finding must not create an avoidable round.
+
+### 5. Shadow gate and break-fix lane
+
+Replay the retained Shepherd operand bundle through:
+
+- the installed merge-authority runtime;
+- the candidate runtime under review.
+
+If an impossible verdict persists after one reconciliation pull or 15 minutes, emit a control-plane incident. If installed authority is defective, pause the product train and use an isolated stable-base control-plane PR. That PR is independently reviewed, merged, verified, and activated before the product lane resumes. Candidate gate code cannot authorize its own merge.
